1
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,608
Hello.

2
00:01:29,608 --> 00:01:31,409
Thank you.

3
00:01:34,174 --> 00:01:35,975
Look at the camera.

4
00:01:46,456 --> 00:01:50,888
You know
what your answer should be, don't you?

5
00:02:11,659 --> 00:02:13,488
Will you marry me?

6
00:02:13,488 --> 00:02:16,448
Say yes! Say yes!

7
00:02:16,448 --> 00:02:19,248
Marry him! Marry him!

8
00:02:19,248 --> 00:02:21,348
Say yes! Say yes!

9
00:02:21,348 --> 00:02:25,148
Marry him! Marry him!

10
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:28,608
Marry him! Marry him!

11
00:02:28,608 --> 00:02:31,728
Say yes! Say yes!

12
00:02:31,728 --> 00:02:36,088
Marry him! Marry him!

13
00:02:36,088 --> 00:02:39,348
Say yes! Say yes!

14
00:02:39,348 --> 00:02:42,403
Say yes! Say yes!

15
00:02:42,403 --> 00:02:45,224
Marry him! Marry him!

16
00:02:45,224 --> 00:02:47,667
Marry him! Marry him!

17
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,688
Say yes! Say yes!

18
00:02:52,342 --> 00:02:54,143
Yes, I do!

19
00:03:15,203 --> 00:03:16,687
She said 'yes'.

20
00:04:12,376 --> 00:04:14,888
Now, you two get the hell out of here.

21
00:04:14,888 --> 00:04:16,138
Go!

22
00:04:21,323 --> 00:04:24,896
I came here with Eva,
and I'm leaving with her.

23
00:04:24,896 --> 00:04:27,688
She will be my wife soon.

24
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,291
Weechana.

25
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,788
If we're serious about getting married,
you need to stop doing this.

26
00:04:32,788 --> 00:04:34,821
I still need to work with them.

27
00:04:35,779 --> 00:04:38,648
I've already found someone to replace them.

28
00:04:40,904 --> 00:04:42,334
Weechana?

29
00:04:42,334 --> 00:04:45,811
I'm working on finding you a new manager.

30
00:04:45,811 --> 00:04:49,328
For now, let Pat handle things.

31
00:04:51,019 --> 00:04:53,408
As for these two bastards,

32
00:04:54,646 --> 00:04:56,832
just let them go.

33
00:04:56,832 --> 00:04:58,624
But...

34
00:04:58,624 --> 00:05:00,648
We're done here, aren't we?

35
00:05:01,254 --> 00:05:03,055
Shall we head home?

36
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,803
I can take you to see your aunt.

37
00:05:11,803 --> 00:05:13,928
You'd like to see her, wouldn't you?

38
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:22,755
Yeah, let's go.

39
00:05:24,011 --> 00:05:25,535
Let's go.

40
00:05:43,056 --> 00:05:44,688
Don't let them follow us.

41
00:05:44,688 --> 00:05:46,012
Go.

42
00:05:47,024 --> 00:05:48,489
We should go.

43
00:05:53,961 --> 00:05:57,068
How many times are you gonna come at us
and lose?

44
00:05:58,616 --> 00:06:00,688
You never learn, do you?

45
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:08,120
Next time, wait until we actually win
before you start bragging.

46
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,982
You're right.

47
00:06:09,982 --> 00:06:12,248
It'll be so embarrassing if we lose.

48
00:06:14,976 --> 00:06:16,777
We're not gonna lose, man.

49
00:06:58,363 --> 00:07:00,006
I'm sorry.

50
00:07:17,635 --> 00:07:19,110
Boat!

51
00:07:22,246 --> 00:07:24,047
Come here.

52
00:07:40,248 --> 00:07:42,568
Hurry. Come on.

53
00:08:18,787 --> 00:08:20,259
Auntie!

54
00:08:20,259 --> 00:08:21,725
Auntie.

55
00:08:25,662 --> 00:08:26,867
How are you?

56
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:29,827
I'm okay. You?

57
00:08:29,827 --> 00:08:31,518
I'm okay.

58
00:08:31,518 --> 00:08:33,693
Eva, come on.

59
00:08:34,318 --> 00:08:37,126
Do you really think I'm such a bad person?

60
00:08:37,126 --> 00:08:40,475
I'm begging you. Please leave my aunt alone.

61
00:08:40,475 --> 00:08:43,040
I haven't done anything.

62
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,870
I just brought you here so you and your aunt

63
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:50,288
could pack your things and come live with me.

64
00:08:50,968 --> 00:08:52,769
Aunt Da.

65
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:57,283
I need to ask you a favor.

66
00:08:57,283 --> 00:09:01,048
You need to stop selling food.

67
00:09:01,656 --> 00:09:03,092
Okay?

68
00:09:15,827 --> 00:09:18,472
Go pack your things.

69
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:24,530
I...

70
00:09:26,011 --> 00:09:28,209
Can you give me three days?

71
00:09:31,107 --> 00:09:34,174
Everything's happening so fast,

72
00:09:34,174 --> 00:09:36,488
and I haven't had time
to get everything in order yet.

73
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:42,361
I've actually got everything ready for you
at my place.

74
00:09:43,976 --> 00:09:47,902
There's a gym, a personal trainer,
and a tutor.

75
00:09:47,902 --> 00:09:50,595
They're all ready to start.

76
00:09:50,595 --> 00:09:54,830
If you need any clothes or anything else,

77
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:57,227
I can just buy you new ones.

78
00:09:57,227 --> 00:09:59,208
It's not about that.

79
00:09:59,878 --> 00:10:03,648
I'm going to be really busy
for the next few days.

80
00:10:03,648 --> 00:10:07,808
If I have to spend time packing,
I won't have time to get myself ready.

81
00:10:08,776 --> 00:10:11,048
And I need time to adjust, too.

82
00:10:11,678 --> 00:10:14,588
I want everyone to see
that it is all over now.

83
00:10:14,588 --> 00:10:17,992
There's nothing going on anymore,
so we can all move on.

84
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:21,075
Foreign film crews
don't want to deal with this kind of drama.

85
00:10:21,075 --> 00:10:23,208
They think it's unprofessional.

86
00:10:23,902 --> 00:10:27,009
I want to show them that I'm ready.

87
00:10:27,009 --> 00:10:29,361
And I need to show them
that I'm the best choice.

88
00:10:37,907 --> 00:10:39,437
All right, then.

89
00:10:40,403 --> 00:10:42,906
I'll give you one day.

90
00:10:45,883 --> 00:10:48,112
I'll come pick you up tomorrow.

91
00:10:49,048 --> 00:10:50,814
And like I said,

92
00:10:50,814 --> 00:10:54,208
if you need anything, just tell me.
I'll take care of it.

93
00:10:55,163 --> 00:10:57,411
Anything you want,

94
00:10:57,411 --> 00:10:59,212
except Pun.

95
00:11:01,438 --> 00:11:03,239
Are we clear?

96
00:11:04,504 --> 00:11:05,982
Yes.

97
00:11:05,982 --> 00:11:07,783
Thank you.

98
00:11:08,648 --> 00:11:10,449
Good girl.

99
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:15,239
Let's go.

100
00:11:36,499 --> 00:11:39,718
Keep an eye on her from a distance
until tomorrow.

101
00:11:39,718 --> 00:11:43,328
If that bastard Pun shows his face again,

102
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:44,763
take care of him.

103
00:11:44,763 --> 00:11:46,227
Yes, sir.

104
00:11:58,344 --> 00:12:00,608
Let's look around this place.

105
00:12:17,608 --> 00:12:20,108
Auntie, hurry up and pack.
Take only what you need.

106
00:12:20,108 --> 00:12:22,187
- We have to get out of here.
- Okay.

107
00:12:32,768 --> 00:12:34,328
Oh, it's you.

108
00:12:37,728 --> 00:12:39,476
You can't leave yet.

109
00:12:39,476 --> 00:12:41,528
Weechana has his men watching the place.

110
00:12:51,661 --> 00:12:53,462
Thank you.

111
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:58,568
I didn't think you two would actually come.

112
00:13:00,368 --> 00:13:02,169
I will never leave you.

113
00:13:22,675 --> 00:13:24,476
It's going to be okay.

114
00:13:25,379 --> 00:13:29,102
Weechana can send as many men as he wants.

115
00:13:29,102 --> 00:13:32,832
They still won't be able to beat us.

116
00:13:32,832 --> 00:13:34,633
Don't you worry.

117
00:13:38,139 --> 00:13:40,440
You...

118
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,427
Are you two really okay?

119
00:13:43,427 --> 00:13:45,006
We're okay.

120
00:13:45,006 --> 00:13:46,807
Are you and your aunt okay?

121
00:13:55,366 --> 00:13:57,568
What about Grandpa Rueang?
Did he come to keep you company?

122
00:13:57,568 --> 00:14:00,800
They kicked him out, shut down the shop,

123
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:04,618
and forced me at gunpoint to call her.

124
00:14:06,955 --> 00:14:09,088
So that's why you said yes?

125
00:14:10,064 --> 00:14:11,619
That's right.

126
00:14:13,672 --> 00:14:15,473
Damn.

127
00:14:16,414 --> 00:14:20,318
How can he be such a fucking asshole?

128
00:14:20,318 --> 00:14:22,368
Where are you running to?

129
00:14:24,088 --> 00:14:27,289
I don't know, but I have to get out of here.

130
00:14:28,131 --> 00:14:31,728
Once he gets me into his house,
I know I won't be able to leave.

131
00:14:35,816 --> 00:14:38,400
Then you and your aunt
should go pack your things.

132
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:41,928
I'll call Ekachai and see if he can help us.

133
00:14:42,843 --> 00:14:44,644
- Let's go.
- Come on.

134
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,120
[Weechana surprises Eva
with a proposal at an event.]

135
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:55,456
What is going on?

136
00:14:55,456 --> 00:14:58,420
I said he could propose to her, but not now!

137
00:14:58,422 --> 00:15:01,046
You're starting to lose your grip
on Weechana.

138
00:15:05,499 --> 00:15:07,300
Did you know about this?

139
00:15:10,818 --> 00:15:13,910
I'm supposed to be the distraction,
not the one creating the problem.

140
00:15:13,910 --> 00:15:15,948
Then go create a distraction.

141
00:15:17,195 --> 00:15:19,368
We don't need to do anything about it.

142
00:15:21,029 --> 00:15:23,376
Hey, what is your plan?

143
00:15:23,376 --> 00:15:27,128
I thought your dad told you
to stick to the plan from now on.

144
00:15:27,128 --> 00:15:31,360
- What the hell is this?
- Nothing's gone off-plan, Grandma.

145
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,968
And you're the one who approved it.

146
00:15:35,395 --> 00:15:39,539
The marriage is supposed
to bury the Domino story,

147
00:15:39,539 --> 00:15:42,923
not distract people from the campaign.

148
00:15:42,923 --> 00:15:45,072
We have to make the public see

149
00:15:45,072 --> 00:15:49,147
that their concerns are our highest priority.

150
00:15:49,147 --> 00:15:51,734
And after this, who's going to trust us?

151
00:15:51,734 --> 00:15:52,963
Where the hell is she?

152
00:15:52,963 --> 00:15:56,040
She said yes to marrying you.
So why haven't you brought her home?

153
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,867
She said she needed some time to get ready,

154
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:00,728
so I gave her until tomorrow.

155
00:16:00,728 --> 00:16:02,347
What does she need so much time
to prepare for?

156
00:16:02,347 --> 00:16:03,400
After the proposal,

157
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,766
I saw you had people
take care of everything for her.

158
00:16:05,766 --> 00:16:08,038
She has her aunt, and her work.

159
00:16:08,038 --> 00:16:10,562
- And you believed her?
- I sent my guys to watch her.

160
00:16:10,562 --> 00:16:13,014
For God's sake!

161
00:16:13,014 --> 00:16:16,582
Can you just be a normal grandma
and do what grandmas do?

162
00:16:16,582 --> 00:16:18,960
Go knit or play bingo.

163
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:20,240
Let me deal with this.

164
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,629
Weechana!

165
00:16:22,966 --> 00:16:24,928
Whoa, bro!

166
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,368
Listen!

167
00:16:27,368 --> 00:16:29,138
If you won't take my advice,

168
00:16:29,138 --> 00:16:30,888
then you'd better know what you're doing.

169
00:16:30,888 --> 00:16:34,368
If you screw this up,
I'll have all your heads.

170
00:16:43,539 --> 00:16:45,547
I know, I know.

171
00:16:45,547 --> 00:16:47,568
I'll apologize later.

172
00:16:51,896 --> 00:16:53,373
Weechana.

173
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:58,528
Are you sure Eva won't try to leave?

174
00:17:06,763 --> 00:17:08,144
Got it.

175
00:17:08,144 --> 00:17:09,945
Thank you so much.

176
00:17:10,608 --> 00:17:12,102
Let me help you with that.

177
00:17:12,102 --> 00:17:13,428
Thanks.

178
00:17:17,624 --> 00:17:19,267
What did he say?

179
00:17:19,267 --> 00:17:21,566
He'll be here soon with another cop,

180
00:17:21,566 --> 00:17:23,704
but all they can do is distract them.

181
00:17:23,704 --> 00:17:26,611
We'll have to use that chance
to escape through the back of the shop.

182
00:17:26,611 --> 00:17:28,104
You hold on to the car keys.

183
00:17:28,104 --> 00:17:30,323
We'll go with Aunt Da
and take everything with us.

184
00:17:30,323 --> 00:17:33,966
If you and your aunt get to the car first
and anything happens,

185
00:17:33,966 --> 00:17:35,891
drive away immediately.

186
00:17:35,891 --> 00:17:37,400
Don't wait for us. We'll be fine.

187
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,656
Ekachai will be there with us.

188
00:17:39,656 --> 00:17:41,808
Do you know where you'll go?

189
00:17:42,718 --> 00:17:46,670
I have no idea.
Probably a hotel somewhere out of town.

190
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:48,179
It's too much traffic.

191
00:17:48,179 --> 00:17:50,128
Someone could recognize you.

192
00:17:50,910 --> 00:17:55,086
If you and your aunt don't mind,
I know a place.

193
00:17:55,086 --> 00:17:57,475
A friend of mine moved back here
after he got married

194
00:17:57,475 --> 00:17:59,448
and opened a café in Khao Yai.

195
00:17:59,448 --> 00:18:00,970
He's got a place we can stay.

196
00:18:00,970 --> 00:18:02,462
It's private and low-key.

197
00:18:02,462 --> 00:18:05,160
We could go there, if you're okay with it.

198
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,307
Okay, let's go there.

199
00:18:06,307 --> 00:18:08,288
Good. I'll let him know right now.

200
00:18:08,288 --> 00:18:11,731
Eva, I think you should leave without me.

201
00:18:11,731 --> 00:18:13,059
I don't want to be a burden.

202
00:18:13,059 --> 00:18:15,560
No. We have to go together.

203
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:19,294
If you stay here, they'll just take you.

204
00:18:19,294 --> 00:18:21,448
I know about that.

205
00:18:21,448 --> 00:18:24,899
I'll just be a burden if I go with you.

206
00:18:24,899 --> 00:18:26,467
Auntie.

207
00:18:26,467 --> 00:18:28,419
You've never been a burden to me.

208
00:18:28,419 --> 00:18:30,808
I'm the one who's put you through all this.

209
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,320
[We're here.]
Standby.

210
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:39,414
I hate to rush you,
but we need to get out of here.

211
00:18:39,414 --> 00:18:40,534
Please come with us.

212
00:18:40,534 --> 00:18:42,395
- But...
- How about this?

213
00:18:42,395 --> 00:18:44,190
We all leave together,

214
00:18:44,190 --> 00:18:48,088
then you can drop Aunt Da and me off
at my place in Saraburi first.

215
00:18:48,088 --> 00:18:50,089
My mom runs a small restaurant there.

216
00:18:50,089 --> 00:18:51,822
Aunt Da can stay with us, no problem.

217
00:18:51,822 --> 00:18:54,850
And I'll stay with her so she won't be alone.

218
00:18:54,850 --> 00:18:56,158
Sounds good?

219
00:18:56,158 --> 00:18:58,288
Please come with us, Auntie.

220
00:19:00,291 --> 00:19:04,008
My mom's cooking is just as good as yours.

221
00:19:04,008 --> 00:19:05,530
Okay?

222
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:10,778
Fine, I'm coming with you.

223
00:19:10,778 --> 00:19:13,483
- Let's go.
- Hurry!

224
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:18,289
What are you doing here?

225
00:19:19,038 --> 00:19:21,632
You've been lurking around here,
watching someone else's house.

226
00:19:21,632 --> 00:19:23,179
You're freaking out the neighbors.

227
00:19:23,179 --> 00:19:25,688
That's why they called the cops.

228
00:19:26,408 --> 00:19:28,227
Exactly.

229
00:19:28,227 --> 00:19:30,382
He said you're not from around here.

230
00:19:30,382 --> 00:19:32,046
Wait a second.

231
00:19:32,046 --> 00:19:34,448
You two look familiar.

232
00:19:34,448 --> 00:19:36,948
I feel like I've seen you somewhere before.

233
00:19:38,148 --> 00:19:40,654
Let me check.

234
00:19:40,654 --> 00:19:42,455
Do you have a record?

235
00:19:49,046 --> 00:19:50,968
They are working for me.

236
00:19:51,595 --> 00:19:53,883
Is everything okay.

237
00:19:53,883 --> 00:19:58,160
Eva told me she's been feeling uneasy

238
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:00,587
because someone's been stalking her lately.

239
00:20:00,587 --> 00:20:03,148
So I had my men keep an eye on her place.

240
00:20:06,986 --> 00:20:09,968
Which house reported them, Captain?

241
00:20:17,899 --> 00:20:19,948
Will you excuse me?

242
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:29,200
[Weechana's at the front.
His men are at the back.]

243
00:20:29,808 --> 00:20:31,744
Let's go.

244
00:20:31,744 --> 00:20:33,003
Watch your step.

245
00:20:33,003 --> 00:20:36,159
Weechana's waiting out front
while his men head around back.

246
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:39,480
Boat, if I don't come back in 20 minutes,
take my aunt and go without me.

247
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:41,805
Got it. Let's go.

248
00:20:41,805 --> 00:20:43,768
Hurry up! Come on.

249
00:20:52,448 --> 00:20:54,683
Eva.

250
00:20:54,683 --> 00:20:56,484
Eva!

251
00:21:01,808 --> 00:21:03,787
Eva!

252
00:21:03,787 --> 00:21:05,588
Eva!

253
00:21:07,905 --> 00:21:09,706
Eva.

254
00:21:11,848 --> 00:21:13,528
Open it!

255
00:21:13,528 --> 00:21:15,329
Hurry up.

256
00:21:21,928 --> 00:21:23,896
You can't get in, sir.

257
00:21:23,896 --> 00:21:26,368
You know this is trespassing, right?

258
00:21:27,656 --> 00:21:29,432
What trespassing?

259
00:21:29,432 --> 00:21:31,656
I have a key.

260
00:21:31,656 --> 00:21:33,736
I just sent my men to unlock the back door.
That's all.

261
00:21:33,736 --> 00:21:36,568
What you're doing isn't legal.

262
00:21:36,568 --> 00:21:38,259
I can arrest you for this.

263
00:21:38,259 --> 00:21:40,142
Stay out of it.

264
00:21:40,142 --> 00:21:41,943
Quit sticking your nose in,

265
00:21:43,376 --> 00:21:46,648
or you might end up with more than
just a suspension. You want to find out?

266
00:21:46,648 --> 00:21:48,449
Are you sure about that?

267
00:21:49,787 --> 00:21:52,878
I can vouch for Captain Ekachai.

268
00:21:52,878 --> 00:21:54,848
He was just doing his job.

269
00:21:57,539 --> 00:22:01,208
Don't you have families
you should be thinking about?

270
00:22:02,451 --> 00:22:03,812
Don't you?

271
00:22:06,723 --> 00:22:08,568
They are not upstairs, sir.

272
00:22:13,768 --> 00:22:15,608
It's none of your business.

273
00:22:18,389 --> 00:22:21,612
I'm about to become part of this family.

274
00:22:23,446 --> 00:22:27,350
I have every right to keep people out.

275
00:22:28,731 --> 00:22:30,532
Anyone goes in,

276
00:22:32,315 --> 00:22:36,208
I'll have them charged with trespassing too.

277
00:22:36,208 --> 00:22:37,544
You.

278
00:22:38,448 --> 00:22:43,568
Trust me when I say your families
will face an even worse fate.

279
00:22:48,504 --> 00:22:50,930
Just pretend you didn't see it.

280
00:22:50,930 --> 00:22:52,731
Go.

281
00:22:53,507 --> 00:22:55,021
Just go!

282
00:23:15,750 --> 00:23:17,551
You need to check outside.

283
00:23:19,670 --> 00:23:23,651
And you, go upstairs and search again.

284
00:23:23,651 --> 00:23:26,128
Check every damn corner.

285
00:23:26,128 --> 00:23:27,614
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

286
00:23:27,614 --> 00:23:29,415
Let's go.

287
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,280
[Weechana, monster from hell]

288
00:24:18,289 --> 00:24:20,090
Fuck!

289
00:24:33,139 --> 00:24:34,534
What?

290
00:24:34,534 --> 00:24:36,069
All clear!

291
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:40,800
[Welcome to Saraburi]

292
00:25:05,203 --> 00:25:06,888
They are not here, sir.

293
00:25:06,888 --> 00:25:09,608
- They are not upstairs either.
- No?

294
00:25:10,803 --> 00:25:13,000
Goddammit!

295
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,128
You can't even find them?

296
00:25:17,894 --> 00:25:19,365
Huh?

297
00:25:46,555 --> 00:25:48,356
Aunt Da, let's go.

298
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:57,425
Be careful.

299
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,715
Auntie.

300
00:26:00,715 --> 00:26:04,299
As soon as I get a new phone,
I'll get in touch with you.

301
00:26:04,299 --> 00:26:07,566
If there's anything you need or want,
just tell Boat.

302
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,862
He'll let me know.

303
00:26:08,862 --> 00:26:11,212
- Sure.
- Don't worry about me.

304
00:26:11,212 --> 00:26:13,128
You need to worry about yourself.

305
00:26:13,912 --> 00:26:18,568
I'm worried about you. He'll come after you.

306
00:26:18,568 --> 00:26:21,883
Just stay safe and come back for me.

307
00:26:21,883 --> 00:26:23,848
I'll be here waiting for you.

308
00:26:25,736 --> 00:26:27,203
I'll be back soon. I promise.

309
00:26:27,203 --> 00:26:29,048
I'll wait here.

310
00:26:32,394 --> 00:26:36,090
Go on, get going before I start tearing up.

311
00:26:42,945 --> 00:26:44,816
Please take care of Eva.

312
00:26:44,816 --> 00:26:48,240
Don't worry. I'll take good care of her.

313
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:50,902
- Please take care of my aunt.
- Sure, don't worry.

314
00:26:51,732 --> 00:26:53,533
I'll see you later.

315
00:27:31,212 --> 00:27:34,044
My friend, my friend.

316
00:27:34,044 --> 00:27:37,420
- Jimmy.
- Long time no see.

317
00:27:37,420 --> 00:27:39,809
- I'm really glad you came.
- Nice to see you, man.

318
00:27:39,809 --> 00:27:41,622
Is this your girlfriend? Hi.

319
00:27:41,622 --> 00:27:43,382
I'm Jim. Nice to meet you.

320
00:27:43,382 --> 00:27:45,082
Hi, I'm Eva. Nice to meet you, too.

321
00:27:45,082 --> 00:27:47,007
I'm Pun's friend.

322
00:27:47,007 --> 00:27:50,302
Just friends... for now?

323
00:27:50,302 --> 00:27:53,168
Okay, okay. Enough with the teasing.

324
00:27:53,168 --> 00:27:55,974
Seriously, though,
thank you for letting us stay here.

325
00:27:55,974 --> 00:27:57,846
- We're really in trouble.
- Yeah, no worries.

326
00:27:57,846 --> 00:27:59,881
But I do have to let you know one thing.

327
00:27:59,881 --> 00:28:02,222
I only have one guest room,

328
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:04,244
and you guys will have to share it.

329
00:28:04,244 --> 00:28:07,625
But the good news is
that it'll be just you two.

330
00:28:07,625 --> 00:28:09,892
The restaurant
gets customers sometimes but...

331
00:28:09,892 --> 00:28:11,604
it's in a different area.

332
00:28:11,604 --> 00:28:13,111
Okay.

333
00:28:13,111 --> 00:28:14,452
Well, he said...

334
00:28:14,452 --> 00:28:16,681
It's okay. I think I got what he said.

335
00:28:16,681 --> 00:28:20,905
He said there's only one guest room
in his house,

336
00:28:20,905 --> 00:28:24,262
so we'll probably have to share.

337
00:28:26,428 --> 00:28:30,358
And good news is the café
and the house are separate,

338
00:28:30,358 --> 00:28:32,790
so we'll still have some privacy.
That's pretty much it, right?

339
00:28:32,790 --> 00:28:34,972
Yeah, you got all of that right.

340
00:28:34,972 --> 00:28:36,773
I'm impressed.

341
00:28:37,701 --> 00:28:40,300
Okay. Thank you for letting us stay.

342
00:28:40,300 --> 00:28:41,510
I really mean it.

343
00:28:41,510 --> 00:28:46,049
And thanks for speaking in a way
that I can actually understand.

344
00:28:46,049 --> 00:28:48,534
What? What do you mean?

345
00:28:48,534 --> 00:28:50,704
No, it wasn't him.

346
00:28:50,704 --> 00:28:52,209
It's you.

347
00:28:52,209 --> 00:28:54,214
He spoke normally.

348
00:28:54,214 --> 00:28:56,015
You're just getting better.

349
00:29:04,681 --> 00:29:06,892
Darling.

350
00:29:06,892 --> 00:29:10,513
Why didn't you tell me
your friends had arrived?

351
00:29:10,513 --> 00:29:12,172
Oh, my beautiful wife!

352
00:29:12,172 --> 00:29:14,780
Come meet my friends.

353
00:29:14,780 --> 00:29:17,004
Hello.

354
00:29:17,004 --> 00:29:21,302
Jim, you never told me
your friend was famous!

355
00:29:23,182 --> 00:29:25,969
- Are you Eva?
- Yes, that's me.

356
00:29:25,969 --> 00:29:28,422
My name is Joy. I'm such a huge fan.

357
00:29:28,422 --> 00:29:30,550
I can't believe I'm meeting you in person!

358
00:29:30,550 --> 00:29:32,294
Can I get a picture with you?

359
00:29:32,294 --> 00:29:34,142
Sure.

360
00:29:34,142 --> 00:29:37,182
Would you mind not posting it, though?

361
00:29:38,340 --> 00:29:41,482
Oh, I heard about that.
If I were you, I'd run too.

362
00:29:41,482 --> 00:29:44,502
He is a powerful man.

363
00:29:47,718 --> 00:29:49,519
Thank you.

364
00:29:51,014 --> 00:29:54,241
Come on, let's go inside. It's hot out here.

365
00:29:54,241 --> 00:29:57,185
Darling, do you want me
to make dinner for your friends?

366
00:29:57,185 --> 00:29:59,153
No, you don't have too.

367
00:29:59,153 --> 00:30:02,262
This is one of the best cooks I know.

368
00:30:02,262 --> 00:30:05,128
- Really?
- We'll let him handle it.

369
00:30:05,128 --> 00:30:06,408
My goodness.

370
00:30:06,408 --> 00:30:09,009
Sounds delicious. I want to try it.

371
00:30:11,385 --> 00:30:13,476
What he said...

372
00:30:13,476 --> 00:30:15,808
about us having to share a room.

373
00:30:15,808 --> 00:30:19,868
Oh, I forgot.
I was just impressed that you understood him.

374
00:30:19,868 --> 00:30:21,121
Jim.

375
00:30:21,121 --> 00:30:22,602
Jim.

376
00:30:31,193 --> 00:30:33,646
Okay, you sleep in here.

377
00:30:33,646 --> 00:30:36,260
I'll take the couch in the living room.

378
00:30:36,260 --> 00:30:38,622
No, it's okay. This is your friend's place.

379
00:30:38,622 --> 00:30:40,408
I'll take the couch.

380
00:30:40,408 --> 00:30:43,977
Back when I was an extra,
I had it way tougher than this.

381
00:30:43,977 --> 00:30:47,102
It's okay. It's been a long drive.

382
00:30:47,102 --> 00:30:50,382
Besides, you're the lady.
You should take the bed.

383
00:31:11,172 --> 00:31:12,973
Can you taste this for me?

384
00:31:15,558 --> 00:31:17,205
What do you think?

385
00:31:19,938 --> 00:31:21,305
Whoa!

386
00:31:21,305 --> 00:31:24,260
Wow, this is incredible!

387
00:31:24,260 --> 00:31:25,348
Hey.

388
00:31:25,348 --> 00:31:29,072
You don't have to teach me English anymore,
you know.

389
00:31:29,072 --> 00:31:31,238
You should open a restaurant instead.

390
00:31:31,238 --> 00:31:32,622
You're exaggerating.

391
00:31:32,622 --> 00:31:34,838
Hey, I am not exaggerating.

392
00:31:34,838 --> 00:31:37,025
I've eaten at some
really good restaurants abroad,

393
00:31:37,025 --> 00:31:38,278
and none of them were as good as yours.

394
00:31:38,278 --> 00:31:39,697
You should open a restaurant.

395
00:31:39,697 --> 00:31:41,502
Have you ever tasted me?

396
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:45,736
I'm talking about your cooking skill.

397
00:31:49,318 --> 00:31:52,209
Actually, like I told you before,

398
00:31:52,209 --> 00:31:55,756
when this is all over,
I think I'll open my own restaurant.

399
00:31:55,756 --> 00:31:58,572
I've managed to save up some money.

400
00:31:58,572 --> 00:32:01,582
Enough for a small place, I think.

401
00:32:01,582 --> 00:32:03,566
Yeah, you should do that.

402
00:32:03,566 --> 00:32:06,022
I will be rooting for you.

403
00:32:06,022 --> 00:32:08,246
One more bite?

404
00:32:08,246 --> 00:32:10,550
Yes, please.

405
00:32:10,550 --> 00:32:12,758
You should try the chicken.

406
00:32:12,758 --> 00:32:13,902
What?

407
00:32:13,902 --> 00:32:16,982
- Let's try the chicken.
- You're not tasting your food?

408
00:32:18,569 --> 00:32:21,462
Any notes? Should I add anything?

409
00:32:21,462 --> 00:32:23,622
Why don't you team up with my aunt?

410
00:32:25,345 --> 00:32:27,182
Working with Aunt Da?

411
00:32:27,921 --> 00:32:29,548
Great idea.

412
00:32:29,548 --> 00:32:32,062
- Fusion food.
- What should we name it?

413
00:32:32,764 --> 00:32:35,409
- Aunt Da...
- Da-Pun? Pun-Da?

414
00:32:35,409 --> 00:32:37,210
Oh my goodness! No.

415
00:32:40,886 --> 00:32:42,902
Wow, it looks so good.

416
00:32:45,932 --> 00:32:47,468
- Alright.
- Here you go.

417
00:32:47,468 --> 00:32:49,468
Wow!

418
00:32:49,468 --> 00:32:51,916
That looks so good.

419
00:32:51,916 --> 00:32:53,007
Thank you.

420
00:32:53,007 --> 00:32:56,318
- Thank you for this meal.
- Yeah, thank you very much.

421
00:32:56,318 --> 00:32:58,144
You're very welcome.

422
00:32:58,144 --> 00:33:00,022
Hey. Cheers?

423
00:33:00,022 --> 00:33:01,262
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

424
00:33:01,262 --> 00:33:03,063
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

425
00:33:08,062 --> 00:33:09,448
How does it taste?

426
00:33:09,448 --> 00:33:13,213
- Really nice.
- This bottle's been aged for years.

427
00:33:13,213 --> 00:33:15,622
Alright, let's dig in!

428
00:33:20,062 --> 00:33:22,692
<i>Several events have been unable to reach Eva
through any channel today.</i>

429
00:33:22,692 --> 00:33:24,782
<i>What are your thoughts on that?</i>

430
00:33:24,782 --> 00:33:26,100
<i>I'm worried about her</i>

431
00:33:26,100 --> 00:33:29,302
<i>because I still haven't been able
to reach her myself.</i>

432
00:33:29,302 --> 00:33:30,598
Darling?

433
00:33:30,598 --> 00:33:33,039
Everyone, look.

434
00:33:33,040 --> 00:33:35,720
<i>What do you have to say
about the rumors</i>

435
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:38,480
<i>that Eva disappeared
after agreeing to marry you?</i>

436
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:42,093
[Eva goes missing after skipping events.]
<i>I honestly don't know either.</i>

437
00:33:42,094 --> 00:33:44,355
But Eva has never done
anything like this before.

438
00:33:53,062 --> 00:33:54,382
Do you think

439
00:33:54,382 --> 00:33:58,102
this has anything to do
with the man Eva's been seen with lately?

440
00:34:01,036 --> 00:34:02,046
Come to think of it,

441
00:34:02,046 --> 00:34:04,982
<i>Eva's life has been a mess
ever since he came into the picture.</i>

442
00:34:04,982 --> 00:34:06,982
<i>Just look at what happened
in that last video.</i>

443
00:34:10,451 --> 00:34:16,297
<i>Could Pun have something to do
with Eva's disappearance?</i>

444
00:34:16,297 --> 00:34:18,729
<i>I wouldn't go so far as to say that.</i>

445
00:34:18,729 --> 00:34:24,862
<i>But one thing I'm sure of
is that Eva isn't safe with him.</i>

446
00:34:30,066 --> 00:34:33,502
<i>If anyone happens to see the man I mentioned,</i>

447
00:34:34,483 --> 00:34:38,942
<i>Pun Punnathorn Jiraworameta,</i>

448
00:34:39,763 --> 00:34:44,447
<i>please notify the police or contact my party.</i>
